+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

TLS pool connections verify the certificate chain using the base-system
trust store and check the configured pool's DNS name or IP address. This
identity check also applies when SNI is disabled. An explicit
"tls-fingerprint" selects alternative trust: a matching 64-digit SHA-256
certificate fingerprint permits a self-signed certificate. Obtain that
fingerprint through a trusted channel. A missing fingerprint does not
permit an unverified certificate.

Run XMRig as an unprivileged user. This port does not provide a pledge or
unveil sandbox. It keeps the secure JIT path, which changes writable code
pages to executable pages without simultaneous write and execute access.
The HTTP API is disabled in the sample configuration; review its listener,
authentication and restricted-mode settings before enabling it.
